      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not entirely necessary. VRChat targets 90 FPS as thats the refresh rate of current VR headsets. If your computer cant do 90 FPS then the game runs at the peak framerate your CPU/GPU combination can render. Also, disabling the frame limiter could have unintended side effects on game stability and cause crashes and render glitches. It also introdu es frame tearing and worsens frametimes, which can introduce stutter, reducing your percieved smoothness.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
