      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bd4da95a5c5264bf3199faf|full_name}: I disagree. The point is having the option to control the processing power the game takes up depending on the situation. Yes it targets 90 FPS but that is only if you are wearing a VR headset anyway. To be frank if you can install and run VR at all you can run the game at 90 fps. \n\nNot everyone can. So having an FPS limiter for when you are afk or if there is a lot of visual stuff going on you can set your FPS to 20 or 60 respectively. \n\nThis would improve quality of life for a vast amount of people who like to socialize but don't have higher end computers. After all if you aren't going to be gone for long leaving the game up is ideal because it does take time to load back into the game and on top of that the world you want to go to.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
