  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Being able to change your max fps to anything you want and also have a framer limiter. A framer limiter would would be useful for desktop as your tabbed out to use less cpu. Mainly for more stable performance and options for people who want to max out their fps or limit it. This should be on by default with a max setting of 60 fps but can go up to 90, with a default of 20 fps for the frame limiter. Being able to change these numbers at any time, but also disable it if you just want max fps all the time.",
